    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 all 32 tests pass, including the new `Cp21Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement for `POST /api/owners` following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**New function class** \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated.java`:\n- Gets an SLF4J logger named `AUDIT` and, in its single `service` method, logs an info line containing the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate` from the `@Val Owner` (already saved, so its id is assigned).\n\n**Wired into the pipeline** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted an `audit` step between `save` and `respond` (`save \u2192 audit \u2192 respond`), under the same `transaction` governance. Placing it after `save` guarantees the owner id exists; placing it before `respond` keeps it on the success path only, so no audit line is emitted when an earlier step escalates.\n\nThe `registrationDate` is logged via `LocalDate.toString()`, which produces the same ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` form the GET endpoint returns (the OpenAPI field is `format: date`), so the test's substring match against the fetched owner's JSON succeeds. Verified output: `AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-08-11`.",
